From: Sameer Tawade <ops@logihertz.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drivers: nvgpu: convert spinlocks to rt_mutex in buffer management paths
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:10:00 +0530

In the out-of-tree NVIDIA nvgpu kernel driver on Tegra234, several internal
DMA buffer management and page table allocation functions hold non-sleeping
spinlocks during multi-page memory allocations. Under PREEMPT_RT, holding a
raw spinlock during potentially preemption-disabled sections creates priority
inversions where high-priority real-time threads are stalled waiting on GPU
allocator locks.

Convert allocator locks from raw_spinlock_t to rt_mutex when compiled with
CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT, enabling priority inheritance and deterministic preemption
throughout CUDA and TensorRT execution.

Signed-off-by: Sameer Tawade <ops@logihertz.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/nvgpu/common/mm/nvgpu_allocator.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/common/mm/nvgpu_allocator.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/common/mm/nvgpu_allocator.c
@@ -102,12 +102,20 @@ int nvgpu_allocator_lock(struct nvgpu_al
 {
 	if (!alloc)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT
+	/* Sleeping rt_mutex with priority inheritance prevents unbounded stall */
+	rt_mutex_lock(&alloc->rt_lock);
+#else
+	spin_lock(&alloc->lock);
+#endif
 	return 0;
 }
 
 void nvgpu_allocator_unlock(struct nvgpu_allocator *alloc)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT
+	rt_mutex_unlock(&alloc->rt_lock);
+#else
+	spin_unlock(&alloc->lock);
+#endif
 }
